<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f4f1e9] text-slate-950">
  <header id="miro-comparison-hero" class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <p class="border-l-2 border-teal-700 pl-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
        RationalGrid and Miro
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight sm:text-7xl">
        Which helps you take an idea further?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
        Miro offers a flexible canvas for working together. RationalGrid focuses on connected
        questions, answers, challenges and sources—so you can return to a specific idea and keep exploring.
      </p>
      <.link
        id="miro-start-cta"
        href={~p"/?focus=grid#start-here"}
        data-analytics-event="comparison_start_grid_clicked"
        data-analytics-comparison="miro"
        data-analytics-placement="hero"
        class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-800"
      >Start a grid <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></.link>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
    <section id="miro-verdict" aria-labelledby="miro-verdict-heading" class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2 id="miro-verdict-heading" class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
        Both help you think with AI. Try the workflow.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Miro includes AI Sidekicks that work with board content, challenge assumptions and suggest
        improvements. Its canvas supports shared planning, workshops and visual collaboration.
        <a
          id="miro-official-source"
          href="https://help.miro.com/hc/en-us/articles/29902701849618-Sidekicks-overview"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-teal-800 underline underline-offset-4"
        >See Miro’s Sidekicks overview.</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        In RationalGrid, select an idea and ask a follow-up, challenge it, or explore its sources.
        Each branch stays attached to the point it addresses. In My Learning, organise grids
        by topic or into collections and folders. Use bookmarks, highlights and search to find
        your place, then continue the exploration with others.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="miro-table-heading">
      <h2 id="miro-table-heading" class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
        Choose by the work you want to do
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto border border-stone-300 bg-white">
        <table id="miro-comparison-table" class="w-full min-w-[40rem] border-collapse text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-stone-100">
              <th scope="col" class="px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold">Your task</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold">Miro</th>
              <th scope="col" class="bg-teal-950 px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-white">
                RationalGrid
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-300 text-sm leading-6">
            <%= for {task, miro, grid} <- [
              {"Plan and brainstorm together", "Arrange and develop work on a shared canvas, with AI assistance.", "Explore a question through connected answers and follow-up branches."},
              {"Examine an idea", "Bring board content into a Sidekick conversation for feedback.", "Attach a question, challenge or source to the exact idea it addresses."},
              {"Pick up the work later", "Continue working with your team on the board.", "Find grids, bookmarks and highlights in My Learning, then return to a specific idea."}
            ] do %>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="bg-[#f8f6f0] px-5 py-4 font-semibold">{task}</th>
                <td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">{miro}</td>
                <td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-700">{grid}</td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="miro-example" class="mt-12 border-l-4 border-teal-700 pl-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">One article. 35 connected ideas.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Explore the grid based on Ignacio Gonzalez’s Philosophy Now article. Choose a point,
        follow its questions and challenges, and see where you would take it next.
      </p>
      <a
        id="miro-example-link"
        href="https://rationalgrid.ai/g/inspired-by-the-philosophy-now-article-a-memetic-664759?node=1"
        data-analytics-event="case_study_clicked"
        data-analytics-location="miro_comparison"
        class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold text-teal-800 underline underline-offset-4"
      >Explore an idea <.icon name="hero-arrow-up-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
    </section>

    <nav
      id="miro-related-comparisons"
      class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-6 border-t border-stone-300 pt-6"
      aria-label="Related comparisons"
    >
      <.link
        href={~p"/compare/chatgpt"}
        class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline underline-offset-4"
      >Compare with ChatGPT</.link>
      <.link href={~p"/compare"} class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline underline-offset-4">All comparisons</.link>
    </nav>
  </main>
</div>
